Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is \u201cfinancial point of view\u201d the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.4. No Solicitation. <omitted> (c) During the Pre-Closing Period, the Company Board may effect a Company Adverse Recommendation Change <omitted> if, and only if, <omitted> (iii) the Company Board determines in good faith, after consultation with the Company’s outside legal counsel and consideration of the long-term strategic value of the offer, that the failure to make the Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law, (iv) the Company has provided Parent with written notice of the Company Board’s intention to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement at least five Business Days in advance, and (v) the Company Board has determined that, after consultation with its financial advisor and legal counsel, the offer remains a Superior Proposal even after considering any modifications proposed by Parent. The Company shall comply with clauses (1) through (4) as follows: (1) prior to giving effect to clauses (2) through (4), the Company Board must have determined that such Acquisition Proposal is a Superior Proposal, (2) the Company shall have made available to Parent the material terms and conditions of such Acquisition Proposal, (3) the Company shall have negotiated in good faith with Parent to amend the terms of this Agreement, and (4) after such negotiations and taking into account any proposed changes by Parent, the Company Board, in consultation with its legal counsel and financial advisor, shall have determined that the Acquisition Proposal remains a Superior Proposal. (Pages 82-83)\nAnswer:
